From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:09:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 131/342] meson_decoder: H.264 with the S905's video decoder

A decoder plugin for the streams FFmpeg's reader describes as H.264, before
FFmpeg's (media_decoder_priority): the chunks go to meson_vdec as Annex B
(avcC streams converted, their parameter sets first), the NV12 frames come
back in display order and are written as B_YCbCr422 (NEON, for the video
overlay) or B_RGB32 (swscale). A frame's time is that of the chunk its
picture is in. Setup() fails, leaving the stream to FFmpeg, if the decoder
is in use, the firmware (system data firmware/meson/vdec/gxbb_h264.bin) is
missing or the stream is more than the hardware decodes (beyond 1920x1088,
High 10, 4:2:2, fields).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
